<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shimazu Yoshihiro</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1535">1535</a>–<a href="/years/1619">1619</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shimazu Yoshihiro was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samurai">samurai</a> general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimazu-clan">Shimazu clan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satsuma-domain">Satsuma</a>, brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimazu-yoshihisa">Shimazu Yoshihisa</a>. He fought in the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a>, won a famous victory at Sacheon during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a> in 1598, and at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sekigahara">Sekigahara</a> in 1600 led his small force on a desperate breakout through the victorious Tokugawa army. Satsuma kept its lands through negotiation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shimazu-yoshihiro.jpg" alt="Shimazu Yoshihiro" width="320" height="314" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 不明。 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shimazu_Yoshihiro.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
